predict_faults(model, snapshots, A)\n\nmetrics = evaluate_fault_detection(df_pred, df_fault_labels)\nprint(metrics)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-01-27T10:55:30.280073Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-01-27T10:55:30.280371Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-01-27T10:55:39.627074Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-01-27T10:55:30.280345Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-01-27T10:55:39.626029Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Epoch 000 | Loss: 0.2721\nEpoch 010 | Loss: 0.1212\nEpoch 020 | Loss: 0.1105\nEpoch 030 | Loss: 0.0988\nEpoch 040 | Loss: 0.0880\n{'precision': 0.0, 'recall': 0.0, 'f1': 0.0}\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":30},{"cell_type":"code","source":"summary_text = \"\"\"\nPHASE 4C — FROZEN\n\nTitle:\nGraph Neural Network for Fault Detection (Binary Classification)\n\nOutcome:\nThe GNN failed to detect injected sensor faults, collapsing to a majority-class\nsolution despite stable training and informative features.\n\nKey Insight:\nSupervised binary classification with BCE loss is insufficient for rare fault\ndetection in sensor networks, even with graph structure and temporal features.\n\nConclusion:\nFault detection requires alternative formulations beyond naive supervised learning.\n\nStatus:\nFrozen. No further tuning will be performed in this phase.\n\"\"\"\n\nwith open(\"/kaggle/working/PHASE4C_FREEZE_SUMMARY.txt\", \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(summary_text)\n\nprint(\"Phase 4C frozen successfully.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-01-27T10:58:03.966046Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-01-27T10:58:03.967097Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-01-27T10:58:03.975099Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-01-27T10:58:03.967055Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-01-27T10:58:03.974100Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Phase 4C frozen successfully.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":31},{"cell_type":"code","source":"","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count"